Arroz Con Pollo
  --Adrianna Adarme

1 tbsp avocado oil
3 lb/1.4kg bone-in, skin-on chicken drumsticks and thighs
1 medium yellow onion, finely diced
3 garlic cloves, minced
2 Roma tomatoes, finely diced
1 medium red bell pepper, finely diced
1 tsp ground cumin
1/2 tsp ground turmeric
1/4 tsp smoked paprika
Saffron threads (optional)
Red pepper flakes
Kosher salt
1 3/4 c short-grain rice, such as Valencia
4 c low-sodium chicken broth, plus more as needed
1 c frozen peas

In a Dutch oven, heat the avocado oil over medium-high heat. When the oil shimmers, use tongs to add the chicken, skin-side down. Sear until nicely browned, ~5 min. Flip and sear the other side for 3 minutes. Transfer to a plate. Lower the heat to medium and add the onion. Cook, stirring often with a wooden spoon, until translucent, about 5 minutes. Stir in the garlic and cook until fragrant, ~1 min. Add the tomatoes and use the spoon to scrape the bottom of the pot. Add the bell pepper, cumin, turmeric, paprika, and a pinch of saffron (if using), red pepper flakes, and salt. Stir to mix all the spices. Add the rice and stir to coat in the tomato mixture. Set the chicken on top of the rice and pour in any juices from the plate. Add just enough chicken broth to cover the rice. Bring the liquid to a simmer, then reduce the heat to low and cover. Simmer until the rice is very tender, 45-50 min, checking every 15 min and adding more broth as needed so the rice doesn’t dry out. Remove from the heat and taste for seasoning. Stir in the peas, then cover and let rest for 2 min so the peas warm through. Bring the pot to the table and divide the chicken and rice among plates.


